{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1396934-elementary-my-dear-lunar-solar-investigation-charms","id":1396934,"title":"Elementary my dear Lunar (Solar Investigation Charms)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-16T13:49:39-07:00","id":1396934,"title":"Elementary my dear Lunar (Solar Investigation Charms)","content":"Trying to write some things after being clawing my way out of the pits that are DFOG, Terraria 1.4, and SRW V/X. Decided to warm on something I already had notes for.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hard-Boiled Detective Stance</span></b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: -\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Investigation 3, Essence 1\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Persona<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: None<br /> <br /> After blowing the lid off countless cases, the Solar has become a seasoned detective in which no mystery is beyond his grasp. The Solar gains the following advantages:<ul><li>Against a target he has profiled a mystery related to a case scene the Solar may ignore up to (Investigation/2, round up) dice of penalties.</li> <li>The Solar increases her Resolve by (Investigation/2) by people who deliberately seek to throw him off a case.</li> <li>Local law-enforcement or authority figures see the Solar as a seasoned detective, treating themselves as having a minority intimacy of respect towards such figures. So long as the Solar is trying to help solve problems that plague the community, the Solar may use Investigation in place of any other social attribute when communicating with such people.</li> </ul><br /> Only one Persona charm at any time (Such as Salty Dog Method) may be active at any one time. The Solar may choose which Persona is active at the sunrise of a new day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Crafty Observation Method</span></b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 5m\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Investigation 3, Essence 1\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Mute<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Watchman\u2019s Infallible Eye<br /> <br /> Add the following text to this charm: So long as the Solar has successfully read at least a single intimacy, they may use this charm to instantly profile a character, allowing the Solar to add (Essence) automatic successes and double 9s to the roll.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Motive-Discerning Technique</span></b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 3m\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Investigation 3, Essence 1\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Linked (Motive-Discerning Technique)<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: None<br /> <br /> This charm functions the same as Motive-Discerning Technique, except that it allows the Solar to roll (Perception + Investigation) for the Read Intentions action. It still doubles 9s and has all of the repurchased contained within the charm.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wise-Eyed Courtier Method</span></b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 6m\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Investigation 5, Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Linked (Wise-Eyed Courtier Method)<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Motive-Discerning Technique 2x<br /> <br /> This charm functions the same as Wise-Eyed Courtier Method from Socialize.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hearing the Whispers of Evidence</span></b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: -\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Investigation 5, Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Motive-Discerning Technique, Evidence Discerning Method<br /> <br /> Even if a person remains silent, the evidence will tell the Solar detective all they need to know. This charm upgrades Motive-Discerning Technique, allowing the Solar to roll Read Motivations against a target he has profiled purely with the evidence presented to him, rather than the target physically being at the location. Only one Read Intentions check may be attempted per piece of evidence, with the sole exception being the repurchases granted by Motive-Discerning Technique. <br /> <br /> Note that the Solar doesn\u2019t have to know the name of a person they\u2019re profiling. As soon as the Solar meets the mystery person they have profiled, they\u2019ll know who they are. If the person is trying to hide themselves (Be it a disguise or red herrings), the Solar may roll a Read Intentions action against the opponent\u2019s Guile. <br /> <br /> Note the evidence can be in any form, be it a physical object or rumors from gossiping townsfolk. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Suspicion Rousing Sense</span></b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 3m\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Investigation 5, Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Mute<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Motive-Discerning Technique, Evidence Discerning Method<br /> <br /> The detective raises their eyebrow as they notice a queer behavior one someone they thought they knew, or someone new showing traits of someone they knew. There\u2019s a reason for that, isn\u2019t there? This charm may be used on a character whom the Solar has profiled, with Watchman\u2019s Infallible Eye triggering a prompt to activate it. The Solar may make a Read Motivation roll against the target, which if successful immediately tells the Solar if the target is under the influence of a Psyche keyword charm, sorcerous influence, or other form of powerful mind-altering magic. Alternatively the Solar may activate this charm to see through the disguise of a character they have profiled, specifically allowing them to bypass any need for senses. This allows a Solar to see through a Lunar disguised as their spouse, even if the Lunar had stolen their form and memories.<br /> <br /> If the Solar knows Crafty Observation Method, it may be activated as a supplemental charm to see through any magical disguises in place of Awareness.<br /> <br /> This charm serves as Watchful Justiciar\u2019s Eye for the purposes of charm prerequisites. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mental Gateway Technique</span></b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 6m 1WP\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Investigation 5, Essence 3\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Mute<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Suspicion Rousing Sense<br /> <br /> <i>Next you\u2019ll say...</i><br /> <br /> Like a Gateway master, the Solar knows what moves her target will make before they even think of them. This charm allows the Solar to declare a fact on a target whom they have profiled, doubling 9s and adding (Essence) bonus dice to the attempt. The declared fact may not go against any currently reestablished information, and while the Storyteller may veto a fact on an NPC they are encouraged to work with a player to determine a way to make such a fact work. A valid example of this charm would be declaring that a Prince will not be attending a gala on the second Evening of Ascending Fire, as because they\u2019ll be visiting their beloved\u2019s grave.<br /> <br /> If an non-playable character uses this on a player character, they roll their Perception+Investigation or relevant pool against the players Guile. If successful they will know one relevant fact or tactic the player will employ in the future. For example, a Solar may already be at a location the players are planning on heading to.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Confessions of the Cornered Rat</span></b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 10m 1WP\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Investigation 5, Essence 4\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Mute<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Irresistible Questioning Technique, Mental Gateway Technique <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CHPd-uLsTV4\" target=\"_blank\"><i><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CHPd-uLsTV4\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CHPd-uLsTV4</a></i></a><br /> <br /> Once the impossible has been eliminated, all that remains is the truth. With their lies exposed and no alibis remaining, the facade of the guilty finally collapses, revealing the truth to all those in witness. This charm may only be used on a target that the Solar has decisively cornered with some criminal act, be it murder or a grevious faux pas on a specific culture. The Solar needs decisive evidence for this to count, such as the actual murder weapon along with the confession of a trusted guard captain who can verify a suspect was not at the location at a specific time. If these conditions are met the Solar may make a (Charisma/Manipulation/Intelligence + Investigation) roll that doubles 9s and (Essence) automatic successes against the Resolve of all those present without any penalty for targeting multiple characters.<br /> <br /> If the criminal doesn\u2019t pay (3 or Solar\u2019s Essence, whichever is higher) willpower then their morale is shattered, confessing completely to the crime they did along with any motivations for doing so. They also gain an appropriate intimacy at a level relative to the crime they did. A convicted man who stole jade to help fund his gambling addiction may have a major intimacy of shame, while a corrupt Regent whose conspiracy to take over the thrown could break down into madness as years of work are forever dashed. If the suspect wishes to attack anyone, they are forced to confess before rolling join battle. If this charm is activated during battle, then battle is paused until the confession is finished.<br /> <br /> Of course, even if the suspect remains silent it bares ill on all those who also hear the claim. The evidence is too damning, their excuses too flimsy, only a blind fool could walk away from such accusations. Any onlookers who see the evidence immediately develop a negative intimacy towards the target proportional to the intensity of the crime. The cost to resist this is equal to (1 + [Highest intimacy towards the target or crime]) willpower.<br /> <br /> If the Solar is wrong somehow, then this charm will not activate. The Solar may use Watchman\u2019s Infallible Eye while preparing for this charm to see if they have enough evidence.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tracing the Spider\u2019s Web</span></b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 5m 1WP\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Investigation 5, Essence 3\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Evidence-Discerning Method, Wise-Eyed Courtier Method<br /> <br /> Crimelords may think they have a moment of respite when the Solar takes down a single member of their network, but the Solar Detective is only getting started. When the Solar takes down an important member within a society or organization, such as a right-hand man or member of a high council, the Solar may activate this charm to immediately treat himself as doing a successful roll against the remaining members in a supernatural burst of insight as dots are connected. This allows the Solar a head start in tracing down any other elements in the group. In case the group suffers dissolution, then this charm still remains active against the ex-members so long as they\u2019re roughly doing the same activities as they were before.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}